                      (    forth6809.asm):02994         ; NONAME (":NONAME", CORE EXT): like COLON, but deliberately skips
                      (    forth6809.asm):02995         ; HEADER entirely - no WORD call (consumes no name from the input),
                      (    forth6809.asm):02996         ; no new header written at DPHERE, and LATEST is left completely
                      (    forth6809.asm):02997         ; untouched. That's the ANS-required "no-name" definition: never
                      (    forth6809.asm):02998         ; findable by FIND, never linked into the dictionary chain at all.
                      (    forth6809.asm):02999         ; In this subroutine-threaded system the execution token IS the code
                      (    forth6809.asm):03000         ; address (no separate CFA indirection, unlike CREATE's DODOES
                      (    forth6809.asm):03001         ; trampoline), so the xt ANS requires :NONAME to leave on the stack
                      (    forth6809.asm):03002         ; is simply CODEHERE at this instant - identical to what HEREW
                      (    forth6809.asm):03003         ; returns - pushed BEFORE compilation of the body begins, matching
                      (    forth6809.asm):03004         ; where ANS says :NONAME produces it. CSP is snapshotted AFTER that
                      (    forth6809.asm):03005         ; push (mirroring COLON's own CSP snapshot, taken after HEADER's
                      (    forth6809.asm):03006         ; transient pushes/pops have already netted back to baseline) so
                      (    forth6809.asm):03007         ; SEMI's control-flow consistency check at ";" only catches a
                      (    forth6809.asm):03008         ; genuinely unbalanced IF/DO etc. left over from the body, not the
                      (    forth6809.asm):03009         ; xt itself, which is meant to still be there when ";" returns.
                      (    forth6809.asm):03010         ; SEMI itself needs no changes: its unsmudge-the-word-at-LATEST step
                      (    forth6809.asm):03011         ; still targets whatever LATEST already was (the previous NAMED
                      (    forth6809.asm):03012         ; word, untouched by this routine) - a harmless no-op there, since a
                      (    forth6809.asm):03013         ; normal definition is already unsmudged by the time any later
                      (    forth6809.asm):03014         ; definition's SEMI runs.
DFD3 DC08             (    forth6809.asm):03015         NONAME:  LDD   CODEHERE
