                      (    forth6809.asm):05041         ; [COMPILE] ( "name" -- )  IMMEDIATE, compile-only. OBSOLESCENT per
                      (    forth6809.asm):05042         ; the ANS standard - POSTPONE (above) is its modern, more general
                      (    forth6809.asm):05043         ; replacement (see POSTPONEW's own header/comment and the GLOSSARY
                      (    forth6809.asm):05044         ; doc). Unlike POSTPONE, [COMPILE] does NOT distinguish immediate
                      (    forth6809.asm):05045         ; from non-immediate words: it always compiles a direct call to the
                      (    forth6809.asm):05046         ; found word's xt, right now, at the point [COMPILE] itself runs -
                      (    forth6809.asm):05047         ; identical to POSTPONE's own PPIMM branch, reused directly here.
                      (    forth6809.asm):05048         ; That's exactly why [COMPILE] was superseded: for a "default-
                      (    forth6809.asm):05049         ; compilation" word (one whose own compiling behavior is itself
                      (    forth6809.asm):05050         ; CREATEd/DOES>-built rather than a fixed JSR, e.g. many words built
                      (    forth6809.asm):05051         ; via : NAME CREATE , DOES> ... ; IMMEDIATE patterns), compiling a
                      (    forth6809.asm):05052         ; direct call to it here is not always equivalent to appending its
                      (    forth6809.asm):05053         ; real compilation semantics - POSTPONE's two-level LIT+COMPILE,
                      (    forth6809.asm):05054         ; mechanism (see PPFOUND above) is needed for full generality.
                      (    forth6809.asm):05055         ; [COMPILE] remains correct for the ordinary case (works on any
                      (    forth6809.asm):05056         ; word whose compilation semantics really is "compile a call to me"
                      (    forth6809.asm):05057         ; - true of every immediate word in this implementation, and of
                      (    forth6809.asm):05058         ; every plain/non-immediate word by definition) - ANS Annex F's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):05059         ; F.6.2.2530 test (13_compiling_words.tests.fs) exercises exactly
                      (    forth6809.asm):05060         ; that ordinary case (DUP, a user-defined immediate word, and IF).
