                      (    forth6809.asm):07317                                  ; after PULU - PULU doesn't affect condition
                      (    forth6809.asm):07318                                  ; codes on genuine 6809 (same class as STOD's
                      (    forth6809.asm):07319                                  ; own fix elsewhere in this file), so BPL was
                      (    forth6809.asm):07320                                  ; testing whatever flags an unrelated, earlier
                      (    forth6809.asm):07321                                  ; instruction happened to leave set, not the
                      (    forth6809.asm):07322                                  ; sign of the value just popped. TSTA
                      (    forth6809.asm):07323                                  ; explicitly tests D's high byte immediately
                      (    forth6809.asm):07324                                  ; before the branch that depends on it. The
                      (    forth6809.asm):07325                                  ; four existing internal callers (DOT/DOTR/
                      (    forth6809.asm):07326                                  ; DDOT/DDOTR, i.e. . / .R / D. / D.R) were
                      (    forth6809.asm):07327                                  ; accidentally unaffected - each happens to
                      (    forth6809.asm):07328                                  ; run "LDD SAVEN" (a flag-setting load of the
                      (    forth6809.asm):07329                                  ; true signed value) immediately before PSHU
                      (    forth6809.asm):07330                                  ; D/JSR SIGN, and PSHU doesn't disturb flags -
                      (    forth6809.asm):07331                                  ; but this was fragile, caller-side luck, not
                      (    forth6809.asm):07332                                  ; SIGN being correct on its own. Confirmed via
                      (    forth6809.asm):07333                                  ; MAME: a direct, standalone use of SIGN (not
                      (    forth6809.asm):07334                                  ; preceded by an unrelated flag-setting
                      (    forth6809.asm):07335                                  ; instruction) never added the minus sign for
                      (    forth6809.asm):07336                                  ; either sign of input.
